From: redC0rvus <111829302+redC0rvus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:29:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] [general] d3d12: --readback_resolve=lazy copies a
 resolve when the CPU first touches it

The resolved guest pages go no-access; the first CPU access (or a physical
free) calls a memory data provider that waits for that submission and copies.
Resolves the GPU already finished are filled at frame start. Exact like full,
but only waits for the resolves the CPU actually reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
